<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Airlines cancels flights to Phnom Penh.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Airlines cancels flights to Phnom Penh.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia Airlines (MAS) announced on Saturday it was cancelling flights to Phnom Penh following the outbreak of fighting in the Cambodian capital.</p>
<p>&quot;Following recent political developments in Phnom Penh, Malaysia Airlines has, in the interest of the safety of its passengers, decided to cancel its flights to and from Phnom Penh tomorrow (Sunday),&quot; MAS said in a statement.</p>
<p>MAS has one flight on Sunday to Phnom Penh, which returns on the same day.</p>
</text>
